<seg id="s0011" group="l0001" targets="p1" role="patient_specific">Diagnosed about 20 years ago based on clinical symptoms (muscle weakness with fatigue, fluctuating
diplopia, and ptosis), presence of antiacetylcholine receptor (AChR) antibody and electrophysiologic
abnormalities (single fiber EMG). At present considered in remission based on clinical symptoms,
negative AChR antibody testing, and normal electrophysiologic assessment (single fiber EMG and
repetitive nerve stimulation) on 2 different occasions. Multiple chest CT scans were negative for thymic
abnormalities.</seg>

